def get_median(nums1, nums2, n):
    # If n is even, the median is the average of the two middle elements
    if n % 2 == 0:
        median1 = max(nums1[n // 2 - 1], nums2[n // 2 - 1])
        median2 = min(nums1[n // 2], nums2[n // 2])
        return (median1 + median2) / 2.0
    # If n is odd, the median is the middle element
    else:
        return max(nums1[n // 2], nums2[n // 2])
```

